 [- capability-GRANTED SERVER lane — these prims (listen / serve / accept-iter
    / exchange-request / respond) are now REAL: listen/serve bind a real net
    listener, accept-iter pulls real connections, exchange-request parses a real
    request off the wire, respond serializes + writes a real response. None of
    that is a deterministic pure-eval result (nondeterministic handle ids, a
    bound socket that lingers across cases, a live peer connection + a [?for]
    consumer), so the granted-lane round-trips live in the BEHAVIORAL gate over
    real loopback sockets — vcx/tests/v08_http_server_real_test.v (low-level
    listen/accept-iter/exchange-request/respond echo) and
    vcx/tests/v08_net_real_socket_test.v (the net layer underneath). The stub-
    era granted fixtures (http-059/060/061/062/064, which asserted synthetic
    shapes) were retired when the impl became real. Only the deterministic
    call-shape check that does NOT touch a socket remains here: stop on an
    unregistered handle is idempotent → null (http-063). -]

 [case id=http-063-stop-granted-null level=core
  [tags http stop granted null]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/http']
[$http:stop [http-server url='tcp://0.0.0.0:8080' state=listening]]
#]]
  [out-text [#
null
#]]
 ]
