 [- §3.6 SSE GRANTED-LANE TRANSPORT is now REAL (held-open sockets), not the
    synthetic `wire=`/fd-less shapes the stub-era fixtures asserted: `sse` writes
    the event-stream prelude and holds the connection; `send-event`/`heartbeat`
    flush real frames; `sse-connect` opens a real streaming GET; `sse-events` is
    a live single-use iterator (frame read + auto-reconnect). None of that is a
    deterministic pure-eval result, so the granted-lane round-trips live in the
    BEHAVIORAL gate over real loopback sockets — vcx/tests/v08_http_sse_real_test.v
    (server push + client read). The shared pure framing/parsing codec's symmetry
    invariant is covered by vcx/tests/http_sse_test.v. The stub-era synthetic
    fixtures (http-073/074/075/076/078/081/082) were retired when the transport
    became real; the deterministic PURE validation/accessor checks (4539/4531/
    4544 + stream-open/source-open/last-event-id) remain below, and one denial
    case keeps the sse-events name covered. -]

 [case id=http-073-sse-events-denied level=core gate=enforced
  [tags http sse-events CXER0271 net-denial]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/http']
[$http:sse-events [sse-source open=true]]
#]]
  [out-err [#
cx-err:CXER0271
#]]
 ]

