[?lib 'cx-stdlib/http']
[$http:send-event [sse-stream open=false] [event data="x"]]
#]]
  [out-err [#
cx-err:CXER4544
#]]
 ]

 [- http-078 (send-event-granted-null) retired: a real send-event flushes the
    framed bytes on the stream's connection, so a synthetic fd-less [sse-stream]
    can no longer return a deterministic null — the live flush is covered by
    vcx/tests/v08_http_sse_real_test.v. The pure pre-flush validation faults
    (empty/CR-LF/closed) remain below + above (http-069/070/077/079/080). -]

 [case id=http-079-send-event-empty-unknown-attr level=core gate=enforced
  [tags http send-event CXER4539 empty-frame hostile]
  [doc [#
HOSTILE (major): an [event] carrying only an UNKNOWN attr has no SSE field
to frame. The prior empty-check `&& attrs.len == 0` let it through and framed
an empty wire ("sent" nothing). It must fault CXER4539.
#]]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/http']
[$http:send-event [sse-stream open=true] [event foo="bar"]]
#]]
  [out-err [#
cx-err:CXER4539
#]]
 ]

 [case id=http-080-send-event-cr-in-data level=core gate=enforced
  [tags http send-event CXER4531 sse-symmetry hostile]
  [doc [#
HOSTILE (blocker): a CR in `data` was framed verbatim then silently stripped
on parse (trim_right), breaking the frame↔parse symmetry invariant. CR in
data is now rejected CXER4531, like id/event. (LF multi-line data is fine.)
#]]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/http']
[$http:send-event [sse-stream open=true] [event data="a\rb"]]
#]]
  [out-err [#
cx-err:CXER4531
#]]
 ]

 [- http-081 (sse-events-frame-too-large, CXER4550) + http-082 (clean-roundtrip)
    retired: sse-events is now a live single-use iterator that reads frames off a
    held-open socket, not a parse of a synthetic `wire=` buffer. The max-event-
    bytes cap (CXER4550), malformed-frame fault (CXER4551), and event round-trip
    are enforced on the live read path (http_sse_read_frame) and covered
    behaviorally in vcx/tests/v08_http_sse_real_test.v; the pure framing/parsing
    symmetry invariant is covered by vcx/tests/http_sse_test.v. -]

]
